WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.824
OpenAI explains how

00:00:01.635 --> 00:00:02.602
it detects and

00:00:02.414 --> 00:00:03.958
disrupts adversarial

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:04.724
distillation

00:00:05.262 --> 00:00:06.736
OpenAI describes how

00:00:06.547 --> 00:00:07.761
bad actors use

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:09.094
frontier model outputs

00:00:08.906 --> 00:00:10.073
to train copies

00:00:09.885 --> 00:00:11.016
without safeguards

00:00:11.158 --> 00:00:11.783
and how it

00:00:11.595 --> 00:00:12.502
fights this with

00:00:12.314 --> 00:00:14.778
testing training classifiers

00:00:14.932 --> 00:00:16.441
API protections and

00:00:16.253 --> 00:00:17.408
investigations

00:00:17.926 --> 00:00:19.647
The November 20 post

00:00:19.754 --> 00:00:20.756
gives the example

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:21.499
of distilling a

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:23.102
model's cyber capabilities

00:00:22.914 --> 00:00:23.857
into a copy

00:00:23.917 --> 00:00:24.600
that will help

00:00:24.412 --> 00:00:25.284
with attacks the

00:00:25.096 --> 00:00:26.593
original would refuse

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:28.112
The average attack

00:00:27.924 --> 00:00:29.055
success rate fell

00:00:28.867 --> 00:00:30.612
from 54.0% against

00:00:30.424 --> 00:00:31.862
GPT6 Astra

00:00:31.886 --> 00:00:32.817
with its original

00:00:32.629 --> 00:00:34.893
safeguards to 0.2%

00:00:34.728 --> 00:00:36.355
against GPT6 .

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:37.428
2 Astra with

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.713
its updated safeguards

00:00:39.246 --> 00:00:40.260
Full story on

00:00:40.071 --> 00:00:40.967
the dashboard
